There&#x2019;s a line in the screenplay of Lebanese filmmaker Rami Kodeih &#x2019;s heist thriller &#x201C;Furies&#x201D; describing how its protagonists, two sisters plotting an overnight bank heist, move as though they are on borrowed time. It reflects as much the film&#x2019;s frenetic pace as it does the experience of living in contemporary Lebanon.

&#x201C;There&#x2019;s an uncertainty day to day, living through a history of conflicts,&#x201D; the film&#x2019;s co-writer Nora Mariana tells Variety . &#x201C;So it does feel like you&#x2019;re on borrowed time, which makes you take advantage of time in a very unique way.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Anya Taylor-Joy ‘Went Mute’ on ‘Lord of the Rings: The Hunt for Gollum’ Set When Ian McKellen Showed Up: ‘That’s F---ing Gandalf’

Kodeih&#x2019;s feature debut, Lebanon&#x2019;s official submission for the 2027 Oscars , screened at the second edition of the Doha Film Festival . The husband and wife creative duo channel the collective anger and anxieties born of Lebanon&#x2019;s economic collapse through a genre they have long loved &#x2014; the heist.

&#x201C;We love it because there&#x2019;s always a reason for why the main characters in a heist film are committing the heist,&#x201D; says Kodeih, citing such influences as Stanley Kubrick&#x2019;s &#x201C;The Killing,&#x201D; Jules Dassin&#x2019;s &#x201C;Rififi&#x201D; and Jean-Pierre Melville&#x2019;s &#x201C;Le Cercle Rouge.&#x201D;

In &#x201C;Furies,&#x201D; the money the protagonists are attempting to steal is their own. Blocked from accessing her savings to pay for her younger sister Dalia&#x2019;s (Maria Nakouzi) life-saving surgery, single mother Maro (Rym Mroue) enlists the help of a former militia member and a truck driver to stage a daring bank robbery.

The premise was Mariana&#x2019;s idea, born of the couple&#x2019;s own experience when Lebanon&#x2019;s banking crisis erupted in 2019, just as she herself needed surgery. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;Frustration is a very mild word. It was devastating,&#x201D; Kodeih recalls. &#x201C;We were relying on some of our savings that were in Beirut to take care of that surgery. And, overnight, we were prevented from doing that.&#x201D;

Ultimately, Mariana&#x2019;s family was forced to sell her grandfather&#x2019;s home to cover the medical expenses. Seven years later, the couple have yet to recover their savings. &#x201C;In a way, this is one of the biggest heists in history. It&#x2019;s just that it&#x2019;s a government that did it,&#x201D; she remarks.

The filmmakers&#x2019; indignation extends to the political establishment that emerged from Lebanon&#x2019;s brutal 1975-1990 civil war. &#x201C;The same warlords are the ones who, once the war stopped, they became the government,&#x201D; Kodeih says. &#x201C;So that&#x2019;s the irony in all this.&#x201D;

Lingering sectarian divisions surface throughout the film, alongside smaller manifestations of the economic crisis, such as Maro cutting open a tube of toothpaste to get the last of its contents.

&#x201C;If the system is fundamentally unjust, how does that trickle down and affect the lives of ordinary people?&#x201D; Mariana asks. &#x201C;How do they take justice into their own hands? And that&#x2019;s a messy human process.&#x201D;

&#x201C;Does it create fractures within a community or does it create solidarity? It does both, we feel,&#x201D; she continues.

Even as they plan the heist, the sisters have to contend with everyday concerns. Maro uses Legos to map out the robbery rather than the traditionally elaborate map seen in the genre, while navigating a custody dispute over her son. &#x201C;The whole point is, how would ordinary people pull off such an extraordinary situation?&#x201D; Kodeih says. &#x201C;To survive,&#x201D; Mariana interjects.

Balancing the film&#x2019;s political and emotional weight with the thrills and humor of the genre came naturally to Kodeih. &#x201C;Once the characters are solid and are human beings, they&#x2019;re not figures. They&#x2019;re just human beings that could exist outside of the film&#x2019;s world,&#x201D; he explains.

Kodeih, who also edited the entire film, assembled some 300 pages of shot lists before filming. The eclectic soundtrack reflects his own musical upbringing, from his conservatory training and experience playing percussion in a school band to listening to his father&#x2019;s collection of classical music records. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The film was equally personal for much of the crew, most of whom had also lost access to their savings. &#x201C;This was the hardest moment of our lives when the bank crisis happened, as a couple,&#x201D; Mariana reflects. &#x201C;This film is an act of resilience and catharsis.&#x201D;

A month into pre-production in the fall of 2024, the filmmakers were forced to halt preparations and evacuate as Israel escalated its bombing campaign against Lebanon. Mariana attributes some of the actors&#x2019; on-screen chemistry to the experience of living through a war together. Amid the bombardment in Beirut, the group sought refuge through watching films together, shutting out the sounds of the airstrikes that resonated outside. &#x201C;You&#x2019;re just realizing what an amazing art form this is,&#x201D; she says. &#x201C;It&#x2019;s helping us survive.&#x201D;

During filming in 2025, the first assistant director alerted the filmmakers to imminent Israeli airstrikes nearby. The decision to continue filming was a collective one. &#x201C;There is a very unique energy on set of, like, we want to make something meaningful. We want to make something beautiful, despite what&#x2019;s happening in the world around us,&#x201D; Mariana recalls.

&#x201C;We always appreciated the opportunity to make this feature, but there was this extra respect for the art form because it helped us get through a really difficult time.&#x201D;

The Lebanese-Brazilian co-production hails from RT Features and Nausika Films, with Rodrigo Teixeira and Berta Marchiori producing. According to Mariana, Teixeira connected with the screenplay in light of Brazil&#x2019;s own banking crisis in the early 1990s. George Clooney and Grant Heslov joined as executive producers after the filmmakers shared a cut with their production company, Smokehouse Pictures. Le Pacte handles worldwide sales and French distribution, with The Plot Pictures distributing in MENA and Vertigo Releasing in the U.K.

It isn&#x2019;t necessarily a recession indicator when cinema resorts to 19th-century IP, but the raft of recent Victor Hugo and Alexandre Dumas adaptations ("The Count of Monte Cristo," "The Three Musketeers," "Les Mis&#xE9;rables") surely doesn&#x2019;t point to a resolutely confident industry either. Now a new film joins these ranks, as director Jean-Fran&#xE7;ois Richet and star Vincent Cassel team up once again for "The Hunchback, Soul of Paris," a bag-securing adventure set within what we must unfortunately term &#x201C;the extended Victor Hugoniverse.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Record Store Day Co-Founder on How Black Friday Evolved Into a Major Holiday for Vinyl Hounds, and What Will Fly Off the Shelves This Year 'Adolescence' Breakout Owen Cooper Stars in New Beatles Music Video for 'In My Life'

For this acts as a prequel to the events of the famous Hugo novel, which has spawned countless adaptations: The author himself appears as a character (don&#x2019;t ask), as does a new iteration of Gavroche from "Les Mis." As the film begins, a voiceover explains sententiously that, at a time when the king of France had recently brought in new laws to crush civil liberties, Quasimodo (Cassel) stands as &#x201C;a man of the people&#x2026; a man to represent the scorned and crushed populace.&#x201D;

But first we must meet the fellow, who at the outset is straitjacketed in a hospice dealing with an outbreak of cholera, where the superintendent doctor (Benjamin Voisin, clocking in for work) believes that the hunchback holds the key to a vaccine, as he is miraculously resistant to the illness. Quasimodo escapes thanks to his superhuman strength (of which more later) and takes refuge within the cathedral, his blue eye reflecting the building&#x2019;s vast rose window before we surge over the ancient city for a money-flaunting title card. Pa-dam! The stakes are set! blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

At this stage it&#x2019;s instructive to remember that both Cassel and Richet originally came to the fore with urgent dramas ("La Haine" and "Ma 6-T Va Crack-er") set in the cit&#xE9;s of Parisian suburbs, which sounded popular unrest among France&#x2019;s dispossessed, chiefly immigrant communities. "The Hunchback, Soul of Paris" ostensibly sides with the people but its approach is perhaps a little less than strictly Marxist-Leninist, as Richet uses his vast budget to indulge in every period drama trope under the sun.

Adopting a formidable declension of every colour from sepia to brown, Richet depicts light streaming through dusty windows; moaning invalids with sores; plucky street urchins; an olde laboratory; a bawdy sex-worker; grimy cobbled streets galore of course; and last but not least, an opulent dinner party, filmed in flat shot/reverse shot, during which two men debate the ethical implications of scientific advancement over the port course. A sure sign of the film&#x2019;s ambient bourgeoisie comes in its treatment of Notre-Dame itself, which we first encounter as an exceptionally hallowed place filled with spiritual light from on high as angelic choirs warble impossibly high notes: Here, you see, is the soul of Paris.

But back to the young doctor, who, you see, believes it is advisable to use the less fortunate in order to benefit science, and to this end orders that Quasimodo be brought to him by hook or by crook, enlisting the help of the corrupt police chief Coco-Lacour (played by Karim Leklou with remarkable commitment and finesse, where a much less engaged performance would have sufficed). There ensues &#x2014; and this is really quite baffling &#x2014; an almost total lack of plot development for the best part of an hour. Instead, we meet Agn&#xE8;s (Daphn&#xE9; Patakia), a young and gutsy street performer with whom Quasimodo falls in love, prefiguring Esmeralda, and observe the titular hunchback as he defends her, scurries around, and lugs huge blocks of marble about the place.

In one of the film&#x2019;s big ideas, Quasimodo is depicted as having superhuman strength, which situates this story about scientists wanting to study his powers in the same lineage as "X-Men" and "Captain America." One suspects that dimension won&#x2019;t send Gen-Z flocking, and it is a rather tired formula overall, giving a handful of fight scenes a wearisome sense of d&#xE9;j&#xE0; vu as the guys getting punched skid a good three further meters along the ground than you might expect. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

As events very slowly begin to grind towards a climactic confrontation, Cassel seems hampered by the main character&#x2019;s make-up and lack of characterization, his performance reduced to a mere bodily incarnation of the hunchback. (A late scene in which he stammeringly bonds with Agn&#xE8;s, on a high rampart atop the cathedral, is perfectly risible and symptomatic of a much wider problem with character-building.) Patakia, as the somewhat modern-minded tart with a heart, is appealing and sensitive enough, but the role is paper-thin. At last, the capturing of Quasimodo sparks a skirmish and Paris starts to burn, but even here Richet feels uninspired, and the battle scenes &#x2014; while handsomely art-directed &#x2014; lack energy and pizzazz. It&#x2019;s left to Patakia, in a bonnet and d&#xE9;collet&#xE9;, to mirror Eug&#xE8;ne Delacroix&#x2019;s "Liberty Leading the People," in a rather mortifying slow-mo that encapsulates the film's general vanity and lack of inspiration.

Veteran TV producer Bob Greenblatt understands why streaming old shows like Cheers or Mad Men is a far more appealing alternative to viewers these days than trying to vibe with a new series.

In an interview with the New York Times , Greenblatt admitted that it's easier to be a producer on an old hit that's enjoying a second life in streaming than it is to launch "a whole new show to the marketplace."

"We're still being pummeled by new shows on every streaming service and rather than try to figure out what's worth committing to, it's easier to just escape into Seinfeld or Downtown Abbey because you know exactly what you're getting," said Greenblatt, who's currently an EP on The Gilded Age. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

